#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:14
msgid ""
"gridsnap, gridsnap-tiler, gridsnap-daemon, gridsnap-editor, gridsnap-picker, "
"gridsnap-hotcorners, gridsnap-ctl, setup-hotkeys - window tiling into zones "
"for Cinnamon/X11"
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: man/gridsnap.1:14
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:19
msgid ""
"B<gridsnap-tiler> [B<--monitor> I<N>] [B<--conf> I<PATH>] {B<list> | "
"B<apply> I<ZONE> | B<move> I<DIRECTION> | B<keys> | B<arrange> | B<stack> "
"I<ZONE> | B<tabs-next> | B<undo> | B<profile>} [B<--dry-run>] [B<--verify>] "
"[B<--quiet>] ..."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:22
msgid ""
"B<gridsnap-daemon> [B<--conf> I<PATH>] [B<--verbose>] [B<--once>] "
"[B<--socket> I<PATH> | B<--no-socket>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:25
msgid ""
"B<gridsnap-editor> [B<--conf> I<PATH>] [B<--monitor> I<N>] [B<--shot> "
"I<FILE.png>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:30
msgid ""
"B<gridsnap-picker> [B<--conf> I<PATH>] [B<--monitor> I<N>] [B<--window> "
"I<XID>] [B<--select> I<ZONE>] [B<--workspace> I<N>|current|conf] [B<--hud> "
"[B<--at> I<X,Y> | B<--follow>]] [B<--grid> | B<--toggle>] [B<--dry-run>] "
"[B<--verify>] [B<--quiet>] [B<--shot> I<FILE.png>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:33
msgid ""
"B<gridsnap-hotcorners> [B<--conf> I<PATH>] [B<--no-hud>] [B<--dry-run>] "
"[B<--verbose>] [B<--version>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:37
msgid ""
"B<gridsnap-ctl> [B<--socket> I<PATH>] [B<--window> I<XID>] [B<--monitor> "
"I<N>] {B<status> | B<apply> I<ZONE> | B<reload> | B<quit>} [B<--raw>] "
"[B<--quiet>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:39
msgid "B<setup-hotkeys> [B<--list> | B<--remove>] [B<--conf> I<PATH>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: man/gridsnap.1:39
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:46
msgid ""
"GridSnap is a visual editor of work-area zones and a window tiler for "
"Cinnamon on X11.  A zone is defined by fractions of the monitor's work area "
"(panels excluded); a window is placed through muffin's EWMH messages with "
"window-frame compensation, so the window frame — not the client area — "
"matches the zone.  Tiling works on top of the stock window manager and does "
"not replace window management."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:59
msgid ""
"The package installs seven commands: B<gridsnap-tiler> (the zone tiler, "
"I<zone-tiler.py>), B<gridsnap-daemon> (auto-tiling of new windows by rules, "
"I<zone-daemon.py>), B<gridsnap-editor> (the visual zone editor, "
"I<zone-editor.py>), B<gridsnap-picker> (an overlay for picking a zone with "
"the arrow keys, I<zone-picker.py>), B<gridsnap-hotcorners> (zone "
"highlighting while dragging a window, I<zone-hotcorners.py>), "
"B<gridsnap-ctl> (the client of the daemon's IPC socket, I<gridsnap-ctl>) and "
"B<setup-hotkeys> (Cinnamon hotkeys, I<setup-hotkeys.py>).  All commands are "
"described on this page; the pages B<gridsnap-tiler>(1), "
"B<gridsnap-daemon>(1), B<gridsnap-editor>(1), B<gridsnap-picker>(1), "
"B<gridsnap-hotcorners>(1), B<gridsnap-ctl>(1) and B<setup-hotkeys>(1) are "
"aliases of this one (roff B<.so>)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:63
msgid ""
"X11 and an EWMH-compatible window manager (Cinnamon/muffin) are required; "
"under Wayland without XWayland tiling does not work. Hotkeys and the editor "
"are part of Cinnamon."
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: man/gridsnap.1:63
#, no-wrap
msgid "COMMANDS"
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: man/gridsnap.1:64
#, no-wrap
msgid "gridsnap-tiler — the tiler"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:67
msgid ""
"The main command: reads I<zones.conf> and moves windows. The first argument "
"is the command."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:67 man/gridsnap.1:247
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<list>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:72
msgid ""
"Prints the monitor's work area (B<--monitor>, 0 by default) and, for every "
"zone, its pixel frame as I<x=… y=… WxH>; the zones go in alphabetical "
"order. Does not touch windows."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:72 man/gridsnap.1:407
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<apply >I<ZONE>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:82
msgid ""
"Puts a window into a zone: the active one by default, B<--window> I<XID> "
"sets the window by hand.  The window's maximization and fullscreen state are "
"cleared, then I<_NET_MOVERESIZE_WINDOW> is sent; the window frame is "
"compensated via I<_NET_FRAME_EXTENTS>.  B<--dry-run> only prints the frame, "
"does not move the window and writes no history.  B<--verify> re-reads the "
"actual geometry through B<xwininfo>(1) and appends \"matches the zone\" or "
"\"does not match!\". A successful B<apply> (except with B<--dry-run>) is "
"recorded in the history for B<undo>."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:82 man/gridsnap.1:412
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<focus [>I<ZONE>B<]>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:98
msgid ""
"\"Only this zone\" mode: the active window (B<--window> I<XID> sets the "
"window by hand) is put into the zone, and the other windows I<of the same "
"workspace and monitor> are minimized (I<WM_CHANGE_STATE> with the value "
"I<IconicState>). Without a zone the window stays where it is — the mode then "
"means \"only this window\". A repeated B<focus> while the mode is active "
"leaves it and restores I<only those> windows that the mode minimized "
"(I<_NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW>, the target last); windows minimized by hand stay "
"minimized, and windows under B<[ignore]> and utility types (dialogs, splash)  "
"are neither minimized nor in the way. B<--off> is an explicit exit for "
"scripts and a second key. B<--dry-run> prints what would be done without "
"moving anything. The mode lives on its own workspace and is not lifted by "
"switching workspaces (restoring is possible only on the active workspace), "
"and it turns itself off only when the target window closes **while the "
"daemon is running**; leaving works from any workspace — the command switches "
"to the mode's workspace itself and restores the windows."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:103
msgid ""
"With B<gridsnap-daemon> running, the command hands the work over to it over "
"IPC (if the socket answers): only the daemon catches windows that appeared "
"after the mode was entered. Without the daemon the mode works once, and the "
"list of minimized windows is kept in I<$XDG_STATE_HOME/gridsnap/focus.json>."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:103
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<keys>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:108
msgid ""
"Prints \"zone, tab, hotkey\" triples from the B<[keys]> section. This is the "
"source for B<setup-hotkeys>. A zone from B<[keys]> that is not in B<[zones]> "
"is skipped with a message on stderr."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:108
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<arrange>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:114
msgid ""
"Takes the client windows from the EWMH list I<_NET_CLIENT_LIST> and lays "
"them out into zones.  Only movable windows are moved: a non-empty "
"I<WM_CLASS> is required; dialogs, splash and other utility types, as well as "
"windows under B<[ignore]>, are left alone. The mode is chosen by B<--by>:"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:115
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<auto>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:120
msgid ""
"(the default) first the windows for which a B<[rules]> rule matched, then "
"the windows without a rule fill the free (not taken by a rule) zones in file "
"order; extra windows stay where they are."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:120
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<rules>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:124
msgid ""
"Only windows with a matched rule, each into its own zone; the rest are left "
"alone."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:124
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<order>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:129
msgid ""
"All movable windows in I<_NET_CLIENT_LIST> order (bottom to top) get zones "
"in the order of the B<[zones]> section; if there are more windows than "
"zones, the extras get the last zone and become tabs there."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:140
msgid ""
"Every window is placed on the monitor it is on. Several windows that land in "
"one zone of one monitor get a shared tab frame: the zone minus a tab strip "
"of B<[tabs] height> (22 px by default). The first window of the list is the "
"bottom tab, the last one the top; a single window in a zone takes exactly "
"the zone, without the strip. The strip with the titles is drawn by "
"I<zone-tabstrip.py> (the daemon starts it); clicking a tab and B<tabs-next> "
"switch the windows of the zone. The previous frames are written to "
"history. B<--dry-run> prints I<window -E<gt> zone: x=… y=… WxH> and moves "
"nothing.  If there are no suitable windows, the command exits successfully."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:146
msgid ""
"When a daemon is running, the daemon applies the layout: the command decides "
"which windows go where and writes the B<undo> history, while the daemon "
"moves the windows, updates its tracker and sends I<window-moved> to "
"subscribers. With B<--dry-run> and B<--verify> there is no delegation: those "
"modes stay local."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:146
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<stack >I<ZONE>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:151
msgid ""
"A special case of B<arrange>: collects all movable client windows into one "
"zone of the monitor (B<--monitor>, 0 by default) as tabs — onto the shared "
"tab frame, like B<arrange>.  A single window is placed exactly on the zone."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:151
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<tabs-next>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:160
msgid ""
"Raises the next tab of the active window's zone. The command lays nothing "
"out itself; it sends a request to B<gridsnap-daemon> through its IPC socket: "
"the daemon owns the tabs, it alone knows which windows stand on the shared "
"frame. The order is bottom to top; from the top tab switching wraps to the "
"bottom one. A window outside zones and a single window are a quiet no-op "
"(code 0), while a daemon that is not running gives a message on stderr and "
"code 1. Usually bound to the hotkey from the B<[tabs]> section."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:160
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<action >I<NAME>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:173
msgid ""
"Runs the action from the B<[action:E<lt>nameE<gt>]> section — the thing "
"bound to a key.  The action receives a window and a zone: the window is the "
"active one (B<--window> I<XID> sets it by hand), and the zone comes from the "
"record's B<zone> field; without it the zone is the one whose frame (or tab "
"frame) the window is standing in (outside zones — none). The window of the "
"subject zone is the active one if it stands there, otherwise the topmost by "
"I<_NET_CLIENT_LIST>; an empty zone means no window.  The screen is "
"B<--monitor>, otherwise the window's screen, otherwise the first one; the "
"grid is the screen profile (B<[monitors]>), then the workspace one "
"(B<[workspaces]>), then I<zones.conf>, as with B<apply>/B<stack>. A record's "
"zone that is not in the grid is a config error (code 3)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:182
msgid ""
"What the action receives: the window, the zone, its pixel frame, the "
"monitor, the workspace, the window's class and title, the config path — as "
"environment variables I<GRIDSNAP_*> (I<GRIDSNAP_WINDOW>, I<GRIDSNAP_ZONE>, "
"I<GRIDSNAP_X>, I<GRIDSNAP_Y>, I<GRIDSNAP_W>, I<GRIDSNAP_H>, "
"I<GRIDSNAP_MONITOR>, I<GRIDSNAP_WORKSPACE>, I<GRIDSNAP_CLASS>, "
"I<GRIDSNAP_TITLE>, I<GRIDSNAP_CONF>) and as I<{zone}>/I<{window}>/I<{x}>… "
"substitutions in the command's arguments. The config path in the command is "
"absolute: the action is started not by the CLI but by a foreign process."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:187
msgid ""
"A custom command (B<run> without I<builtin:>) is parsed by B<shlex> and "
"started B<without a shell and without waiting> (I<start_new_session>): a key "
"must not be bound to a terminal that lives until the window closes. If you "
"need a shell, write I<sh -c \"…\"> yourself. Built-in actions (B<run = "
"builtin:E<lt>nameE<gt>>):"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:188
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<minimize-others>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:194
msgid ""
"The same mode as B<focus>: the window into the record's zone (no B<zone> — "
"\"only this window\"), the other windows of the workspace and monitor "
"minimized, a repeated press restores them.  With a live daemon the daemon "
"owns the mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:194
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<show-window>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:200
msgid ""
"Show a window of the zone: raises and restores the window "
"(I<_NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW>); for a stack, the neighbour on the ring next to the "
"active one. No zone or an empty zone — a quiet no-op (code 0) with a message "
"on stderr."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:200
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<mirror>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:209
msgid ""
"Swaps windows with the mirror zone: the mirror is found by geometry (by the "
"record's B<axis>, I<horizontal> by default — left↔right), not by name. The "
"window of the subject zone goes into the mirror zone, the mirror's window "
"comes back; an empty zone reduces the swap to moving one window, both empty "
"— no-op. Every zone gets a frame according to the number of windows now in "
"it (the tab strip), and the previous frames are written to history for "
"B<undo>. No mirror zone — code 1."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:209
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<terminal>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:218
msgid ""
"A terminal in a zone: the command from the record's B<command> field "
"(I<x-terminal-emulator> by default, substitutions work) is started detached, "
"the new window is looked for in I<_NET_CLIENT_LIST> for up to ~5 seconds and "
"placed into the zone with a frame for the number of windows plus one. The "
"zone must be set in the record (otherwise code 1 with a hint); if no window "
"appeared — code 1 too. The frame is set even when the daemon has already "
"placed the window by B<[rules]>: the action has the last word."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:225
msgid ""
"B<--dry-run> prints the parsed context (window, zone, frame, monitor, "
"workspace) and the plan: for a built-in — what it would do, for a command — "
"the ready I<argv>; nothing is started or moved. Codes: 3 — no such action, a "
"broken field, an unknown substitution; 1 — a refusal on state (no mirror "
"zone, the terminal did not appear); 0 — success and an honest no-op."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:225
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<undo>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:236
msgid ""
"Returns windows to their previous frames from the history: without flags — "
"the last operation, with B<--all> — the whole history, and for every window "
"the frame is taken from the earliest operation it appears in. Before "
"restoring, the window's current I<WM_CLASS> is compared with the recorded "
"one: if the XID has been reused by another application or the window is "
"gone, it is skipped (that is not an error).  Only geometry is restored, not "
"the maximized state; the workspace is remembered, but windows are not moved "
"between workspaces. The rolled-back operation is removed from the history "
"(B<--all> clears the history). An empty history is a success."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:236
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<profile >I<ACTION>B< [>I<NAME>B<]>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:246
msgid ""
"Layout profiles: a complete set of zones, rules, exclusions and hotkeys. A "
"profile is a separate file I<E<lt>templatesE<gt>/E<lt>nameE<gt>.conf>; it "
"contains only the B<[zones]> section (with the bindings from B<[keys]>), "
"B<[rules]> and B<[ignore]>, without B<[grid]> and B<[daemon]>. The name is "
"sanitized by the same rule as zone names; the path cannot leave the profiles "
"directory. An action takes no more words than described below: an extra "
"argument is an error (code 2); the profile name is set by B<--name>, and the "
"second word of B<export> is a file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:250
msgid "Names of saved profiles in alphabetical order."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:250
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<show >I<NAME>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:253
msgid "The contents of the profile file verbatim."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:253
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<save >I<NAME>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:258
msgid ""
"Save the zones of the current I<zones.conf> (with their bindings), its "
"B<[rules]> and B<[ignore]> as a profile.  An empty set of zones is not saved "
"(code 2)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:258
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<use >I<NAME>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:265
msgid ""
"Overwrite in the active I<zones.conf> the B<[zones]>, B<[rules]>, "
"B<[ignore]> and B<[keys]> sections with the profile's contents, keeping "
"B<[grid]>, B<[daemon]> and the other sections. After writing, "
"B<setup-hotkeys.py> is started with the same B<--conf> so that the new "
"hotkeys work; B<--no-hotkeys> turns that off."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:265
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<use-monitors>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:272
msgid ""
"Assemble the active I<zones.conf> from the B<[monitors]> bindings: the "
"B<[zones]> of the first screen plus the B<[zones:E<lt>outputE<gt>]> of the "
"others, merging B<[rules]>, B<[ignore]> and B<[keys]>.  This is how the "
"screen grid is applied at session start; B<--dry-run> prints the config "
"without writing anything."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:272
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<rm >I<NAME>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:275
msgid "Delete the profile."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:275
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<export >I<NAME>B< [>I<FILE>B<]>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:280
msgid ""
"Dump the profile to portable JSON (I<gridsnap_profile>: 1) — as a file or to "
"stdout.  Without a file — to stdout, if B<--json> is given; both at once is "
"an error (code 2)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:280
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<import >I<FILE>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:285
msgid ""
"Load a JSON profile into I<E<lt>templatesE<gt>/E<lt>nameE<gt>.conf>; the "
"name is taken from the JSON, and B<--name> I<NAME> overrides it. The main "
"format remains I<.conf>: JSON is only a portable exchange between machines."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:285
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<gallery>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:289
msgid ""
"List the ready-made layouts shipped with the package: id, title, number of "
"zones and description, one per line; B<--json> prints the same in JSON."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:289
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<from-gallery >I<ID>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:294
msgid ""
"Copy layout I<ID> into your profile: the name is set by B<--name> I<NAME>, "
"by default the layout's id. If the name is taken it is an error: choose "
"another name or remove the profile (B<profile rm>)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:302
msgid ""
"Layouts live in I<E<lt>prefixE<gt>/share/gridsnap/gallery> (in a checkout — "
"the I<gallery/> directory next to the code); the I<GRIDSNAP_GALLERY> "
"variable sets a custom directory.  A layout file is an ordinary I<.conf> "
"with an extra B<[gallery]> section: I<title>, I<description> and an optional "
"I<order> (position in the menu, 100 by default). The gallery directory is "
"never modified: the layout is copied into the profile and lives its own life "
"from then on. In the editor the same is done by the “From gallery…” button."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: man/gridsnap.1:303
#, no-wrap
msgid "gridsnap-daemon — auto-tiling of new windows"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:313
msgid ""
"An optional long-lived daemon: it subscribes to I<PropertyNotify> on "
"I<_NET_CLIENT_LIST> on the root, reads the list through B<xprop>(1) B<-root> "
"and brings the layout into line. Windows that appear are placed by the "
"B<[rules]> rules on the monitor they are on; windows that disappear are "
"dropped from bookkeeping. Utility window types and everything matched by "
"B<[ignore]> are left alone. The daemon remembers the frame it placed in "
"I<$XDG_STATE_HOME/gridsnap/placed.json>: if the user has carried a window "
"out of a zone, the daemon does not return it there again, even after a "
"restart."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:319
msgid ""
"With B<[daemon] reflow = neighbors> the freed zone is expanded by a "
"neighbouring occupied zone within the same monitor, and when a window comes "
"into it by rule again, the neighbour returns to its original frame. A "
"minimized window does not disappear from I<_NET_CLIENT_LIST>, so reflow does "
"not trigger."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:325
msgid ""
"By default the daemon raises an IPC socket (B<--socket> I<PATH> changes the "
"path, B<--no-socket> turns IPC off). B<--verbose> prints what the daemon "
"does.  B<--once> processes one window-list change and exits; if no event "
"came, it waits 2 seconds and exits (for smoke checks). Stop with Ctrl-C "
"(B<SIGINT>) or B<gridsnap-ctl quit>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:334
msgid ""
"The daemon also runs \"only this zone\" mode (the IPC command B<focus>): the "
"window is put into the zone and the other windows of its workspace and "
"monitor are minimized; windows that appear while the mode is already active "
"are minimized by the daemon at once. Switching workspaces does not lift the "
"mode (restoring is possible only on the active workspace); it is lifted by a "
"repeated command, by the target disappearing and by the daemon terminating; "
"the un-restored remainder is written by the daemon to the mode's state file, "
"from where B<gridsnap-tiler focus --off> finishes the job."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: man/gridsnap.1:334
#, no-wrap
msgid "gridsnap-editor — the visual zone editor"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:346
msgid ""
"A GTK 3 window with the monitor's work area at natural scale. A zone can be "
"dragged with the mouse and pulled by an edge or a corner; snapping is to the "
"screen edges, to neighbouring zones and to the 1/4, 1/3, 1/2, 2/3, 3/4 "
"lines. A double click on empty space creates a zone, I<Delete> deletes it; "
"there are layout templates (2 columns, 1 + 2, 2 × 2, 3 columns, main + "
"stack, blank canvas), a name and a hotkey for every zone, a \"Profiles\" "
"menu (save, load as a draft, delete), saving to I<zones.conf>, a button to "
"register the hotkeys and a button to check \"put the active window into the "
"zone\".  The minimum zone size is 5 % of the screen; a zone of zero area is "
"not saved.  B<--monitor> I<N> selects the monitor, B<--shot> I<FILE.png> "
"saves a snapshot of the interface and exits (for checks)."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: man/gridsnap.1:346
#, no-wrap
msgid "gridsnap-picker — the zone picking overlay"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:355
msgid ""
"Shows the zones of the active monitor on top of the work area. The zone "
"under the cursor and the current selection are highlighted; the arrows move "
"the selection by the geometry of the zones, I<Enter> puts the active window "
"into the selected zone (and records the operation in the history), I<Esc> "
"cancels; a left click places, a right click cancels. An excluded window "
"(B<[ignore]> or a utility type) is not moved: code 1 and a message. The "
"overlay grabs the keyboard itself, so the arrows do not go to another "
"window."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:362
msgid ""
"B<--select> I<ZONE> sets the initial selection, B<--monitor> I<N> — the "
"monitor (the active window's monitor by default, otherwise the one under the "
"cursor), B<--window> I<XID> — the window to place, B<--dry-run> only prints "
"the target frame, B<--verify> checks the frame after placing, B<--quiet> "
"does not print the line about the placement, B<--shot> I<FILE.png> draws the "
"overlay to PNG and exits without interaction."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:366
msgid ""
"B<--hud> is the passive grid of the drag watcher: B<--at> I<X,Y> marks one "
"point and exits, B<--follow> reads I<X Y> lines from standard input until "
"end of file or B<SIGTERM>. It takes no focus and no input."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:376
msgid ""
"B<--grid> leaves the zone grid on the live desktop: the frames and the label "
"plates are drawn over whatever windows are open, so the desktop and the "
"windows stay visible; the zone under the pointer is the only accented "
"one. The window takes no input, and nothing is placed. A compositing window "
"manager is required — without one the window has no alpha and would cover "
"the desktop, so the command refuses with code 1. B<--toggle> shows that "
"grid, or hides it again if this desktop already shows one; the grid of "
"another desktop is left alone. B<setup-hotkeys> binds the toggle to the key "
"from B<[overlay]>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:379
msgid ""
"B<--grid --shot> I<FILE.png> writes the grid as a transparent PNG: the same "
"frames and plates without a background, for checks and pictures."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: man/gridsnap.1:379
#, no-wrap
msgid "gridsnap-hotcorners — zone highlighting while dragging a window"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:384
msgid ""
"Dragging a window by its title bar highlights the zone under the cursor, and "
"releasing drops the window into it. It is a separate process: not needed for "
"ordinary work, it does not get in the daemon's way, and the user sets up a "
"hotkey for it themselves (as for B<gridsnap-picker>)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:393
msgid ""
"X11 does not report “a window is being dragged”, so the watcher listens to "
"XInput2 raw events on the root window (they arrive even when the device is "
"grabbed by the window manager) and counts a press in the title bar of the "
"active window as a drag. While the grid is shown, Cinnamon's “throw to the "
"edge” (I<edge-tiling>) is muted so that the window does not jump twice, and "
"it is restored right after the release — the setting is not left off. If "
"XInput2 is unavailable, the watcher polls the pointer about 30 times per "
"second. Details are in I<docs/specs/zone-hotcorners.md>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:398
msgid ""
"B<--no-hud> turns the highlighting off (the window is still dropped on "
"release, I<edge-tiling> is not touched), B<--dry-run> prints what the "
"watcher would do without moving anything, B<--verbose> writes every event "
"(press, HUD shown, I<edge-tiling>, drop) to stderr."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: man/gridsnap.1:398
#, no-wrap
msgid "gridsnap-ctl — the daemon's IPC client"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:401
msgid ""
"Talks to the UNIX socket of B<gridsnap-daemon>: one JSON command per "
"connection, the reply is also a JSON line. Commands:"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:401
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<status>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:407
msgid ""
"The daemon's state: I<conf>, I<version>, I<reflow>, I<profile> (I<null> for "
"now), I<monitors> (work areas), I<zones> (fractions 0..1), I<zones_px> "
"(pixel frames for every monitor), I<windows> (window, zone, monitor) and "
"I<filled> (expanded reflow neighbours)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:412
msgid ""
"Put a window into a zone: B<--window> I<XID> (the active window by default), "
"B<--monitor> I<N>. A success is recorded in the daemon's tracker, so closing "
"the window then starts reflow as usual."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:419
msgid ""
"\"Only this zone\" mode: minimize all windows of the same workspace and "
"monitor except the target (B<--window> I<XID>, the active one by default)  "
"and put it into I<ZONE>; without a zone the window is not moved. A repeated "
"command and B<--off> leave the mode. B<focus> has no B<--monitor>: the area "
"is taken from the target window."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:419
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<reload>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:422
msgid "Re-read I<zones.conf> (grid, rules, reflow); the monitor cache is dropped."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:422
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<quit>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:425
msgid "Ask the daemon to terminate after the current event."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:425
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<watch>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:439
msgid ""
"Subscribe to the daemon's events and print them: one JSON line per event on "
"stdout until the connection is closed (B<Ctrl-C> — exit code 0). The "
"subscription covers all groups (I<window>, I<focus>); there is no option to "
"choose groups. One line about the subscription goes to stderr (B<--quiet> "
"suppresses it). No daemon or a rejected command — exit code 1; a zone, "
"window or monitor in the arguments — exit code 2. Events and their fields: "
"I<window-appeared> (I<window>, I<zone>, I<workspace>, I<monitor>), "
"I<window-closed> (I<window>, I<zone>), I<window-moved> (I<window>, I<zone>, "
"I<previous>, I<workspace>, I<monitor>), I<focus-on> (I<zone>, I<window>, "
"I<minimized>), I<focus-off> (I<zone>, I<restored>, I<total>). I<window> is a "
"hex string, I<zone> is a name or I<null>, I<workspace> is the EWMH workspace "
"number, I<monitor> is I<[x, y, w, h]>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:442
msgid ""
"B<--socket> I<PATH> sets the socket path, B<--raw> prints the reply on one "
"line, B<--quiet> prints nothing on success."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: man/gridsnap.1:442
#, no-wrap
msgid "setup-hotkeys — Cinnamon hotkeys"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:459
msgid ""
"Reads B<[keys]> through B<gridsnap-tiler keys> (and B<[move]> — through "
"B<keys --move>) and creates Cinnamon custom hotkeys (the "
"I<org.cinnamon.desktop.keybindings> schemas) named \"zone-tiler: "
"E<lt>zoneE<gt>\" with the command B<python3 E<lt>code "
"directoryE<gt>/zone-tiler.py apply E<lt>zoneE<gt> --quiet> (with B<--conf> "
"if it is given). The optional B<[focus]> section gives one more hotkey, "
"\"zone-tiler: focus\", for \"only this zone\" mode; it is read from "
"I<zones.conf> by the script itself (through "
"B<zone_config.load_focus_keys>). The optional B<[tabs]> section gives a "
"\"zone-tiler: tabs-next\" hotkey for \"the next window of the zone\" "
"(B<zone_config.load_tabs_config>).  Every B<[action:E<lt>nameE<gt>]> section "
"with a non-empty B<key> gives a \"zone-tiler: action E<lt>nameE<gt>\" hotkey "
"with the command B<gridsnap-tiler action E<lt>nameE<gt> --quiet> (the script "
"installs it itself, like the zone keys). All hotkeys installed by earlier "
"runs (by name prefix) are removed first, so that no garbage is left.  "
"B<--list> only shows the plan, B<--remove> deletes the GridSnap hotkeys and "
"installs nothing, B<--conf> I<PATH> points at the config."
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: man/gridsnap.1:459
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:462
msgid ""
"Keys of B<gridsnap-tiler> (common to all its commands unless stated "
"otherwise):"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:462
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<-h, --help>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:465
msgid "Help on the arguments and exit."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:465
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--conf>I< PATH>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:470
msgid ""
"The configuration file. By default I<$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/gridsnap/zones.conf>, "
"and if it does not exist — I<zones.conf> next to the code. The flag carries "
"the profiles directory along with it."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:470
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--monitor>I< N>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:475
msgid ""
"The monitor number (0 by default). Used by the B<list>, B<apply>, B<stack> "
"and B<action> commands (for an action — the screen on which the zone is "
"looked up)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:475
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--window>I< XID>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:479
msgid ""
"The window identifier for B<apply>, B<focus> and B<action>: decimal or "
"I<0x…>. The active window by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:479
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--off>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:483
msgid ""
"B<focus>: explicitly leave \"only this zone\" mode (restore what the mode "
"minimized) instead of entering it."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:483
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--by>I< auto|rules|order>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:486
msgid "How windows are chosen for B<arrange> (I<auto> by default), see above."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:486
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--all>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:489
msgid "B<undo>: roll back the whole history instead of the last operation."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:489
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--no-hotkeys>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:492
msgid "B<profile use>: do not register hotkeys after activating the profile."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:492
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--json>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:495
msgid ""
"B<profile export>: print JSON to stdout instead of writing a file. B<profile "
"gallery>: the same JSON instead of a table."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:495
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--name>I< NAME>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:500
msgid ""
"B<profile import>: the profile name; taken from the JSON by "
"default. B<profile from-gallery>: the name of the profile to copy the layout "
"into; by default the layout id."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:500
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--dry-run>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:503
msgid "Only compute the frame: do not move the window, write no history."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:503
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--verify>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:507
msgid ""
"Re-read the real window geometry after the layout and compare it with the "
"zone."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:507
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--quiet>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:510
msgid "Do not print success messages (in B<--help> the description is not shown)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:510
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--version>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:513
msgid "Prints I<zone-tiler 0.3.0> and exits."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:516
msgid ""
"The keys of the other commands are listed in the COMMANDS section; each of "
"them also has B<-h> and B<--version>."
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: man/gridsnap.1:516
#, no-wrap
msgid "CONFIGURATION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:524
msgid ""
"The configuration is a single UTF-8 INI file, I<zones.conf>. By default "
"I<$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/gridsnap/zones.conf> is taken (usually "
"I<~/.config/gridsnap/zones.conf>); if it does not exist — the file "
"I<zones.conf> next to the code (I</usr/lib/gridsnap/zones.conf> for a system "
"package). B<--conf> I<PATH> overrides the choice. Comments are I<#> and I<;> "
"(including at the end of a line after a space); the separator is only I<=>, "
"so the key I<re:E<lt>regexE<gt>> is not split at the colon."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: man/gridsnap.1:524
#, no-wrap
msgid "[grid]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:528
msgid ""
"Grid lines: B<cols> and B<rows> — increasing lists of fractions separated by "
"a comma, a space or a semicolon; the last line must be I<1.0>. Needed only "
"by range zones."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: man/gridsnap.1:528
#, no-wrap
msgid "[zones]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:531
msgid ""
"Zone name = one of two forms (zone names are lowercased — that is how "
"ConfigParser works):"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:532
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<x, y, w, h>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:535
msgid ""
"A free rectangle as fractions of the work area: I<0 E<lt>= x E<lt> 1>, I<0 "
"E<lt>= y E<lt> 1>, I<w E<gt> 0>, I<h E<gt> 0>, I<x+w E<lt>= 1>, I<y+h E<lt>= "
"1>. This is the canonical form; the editor saves the file in it."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:535
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<c0:c1, r0:r1>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:538
msgid ""
"A range of grid cells: indices of the B<cols> and B<rows> lines (I<0 E<lt>= "
"c0 E<lt> c1 E<lt>= number of columns>). Read for compatibility."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:541
msgid "At least one zone is required."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: man/gridsnap.1:541
#, no-wrap
msgid "[rules]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:549
msgid ""
"The section is optional. Auto-tiling rules: I<selector = zone name>. A "
"selector is a case-insensitive glob on I<WM_CLASS> or I<re:E<lt>regexE<gt>> "
"— a regular expression (I<re.search>, case-insensitive) on the "
"I<class|title> string. Line order matters: the first match wins. A rule "
"pointing at a zone that is not in B<[zones]> is a config error; an invalid "
"regular expression simply never matches. Key case is preserved in this "
"section."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: man/gridsnap.1:549
#, no-wrap
msgid "[ignore]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:557
msgid ""
"The section is optional. Exclusion windows: I<selector = note>. The "
"selectors are the same as in B<[rules]> (a glob on I<WM_CLASS> or "
"I<re:E<lt>regexE<gt>> on the I<class|title> string); the right-hand side is "
"a note for a human and for the daemon's log. An excluded window is moved "
"neither by the daemon, nor by B<arrange>/B<stack>, nor by "
"B<apply>/B<move>/B<undo>, nor by the picker, nor by the B<zone-hotcorners> "
"drag watcher; it can be moved only by removing the rule."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: man/gridsnap.1:557
#, no-wrap
msgid "[keys]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:560
msgid ""
"Hotkeys: I<zone name = Cinnamon hotkey>, for example "
"I<E<lt>SuperE<gt>E<lt>AltE<gt>1>."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: man/gridsnap.1:560
#, no-wrap
msgid "[move]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:565
msgid ""
"The section is optional. Moving a window into a neighbouring zone: "
"I<direction = Cinnamon hotkey>, the directions are I<left>, I<right>, I<up>, "
"I<down> (the B<move> command). Without the section the defaults apply; a key "
"that is not one of the directions is a config error (code 3)."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: man/gridsnap.1:565
#, no-wrap
msgid "[focus]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:573
msgid ""
"The section is optional. B<key> — the hotkey of \"only this zone\" mode in "
"Cinnamon syntax; B<zone> — the zone the window is put into "
"(optional). Without B<zone> the hotkey only minimizes windows without moving "
"the target. An unknown key in the section and an empty B<zone> value are a "
"config error (code 3). The section is carried over by B<setup-hotkeys> (the "
"name \"zone-tiler: focus\") and by the editor; it is not part of layout "
"profiles."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: man/gridsnap.1:573
#, no-wrap
msgid "[tabs]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:584
msgid ""
"The section is optional. B<key> — the hotkey for \"the next window of the "
"zone\" (the B<tabs-next> command) in Cinnamon syntax; B<height> — the tab "
"strip height in pixels, an integer greater than zero (22 by "
"default). Without B<key> no hotkey is registered; B<height> is read without "
"it as well.  An unknown key in the section and garbage in B<height> (not a "
"number, zero, negative) are a config error (code 3): a strip of zero height "
"is invisible, and the tabs would silently become invisible.  The section is "
"carried over by B<setup-hotkeys> (the name \"zone-tiler: tabs-next\") and by "
"the editor — verbatim, as a foreign section; it is not part of layout "
"profiles."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: man/gridsnap.1:584
#, no-wrap
msgid "[overlay]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:593
msgid ""
"The section is optional. B<key> — the Cinnamon hotkey that shows the zone "
"grid over the live desktop and hides it again (the B<gridsnap-picker "
"--toggle> command). Without the section the default I<E<lt>SuperE<gt>g> is "
"registered; an empty value turns the shortcut off, and the grid stays "
"reachable by hand. An unknown key in the section is a config error (code "
"3). The section is carried over by B<setup-hotkeys> (the name \"zone-tiler: "
"desktop grid\") and by the editor verbatim; it is not part of layout "
"profiles."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: man/gridsnap.1:593
#, no-wrap
msgid "[action:E<lt>nameE<gt>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:596
msgid ""
"The section is optional: one section is one instance of an action, the name "
"from I<[a-z0-9_-]> (the B<action E<lt>nameE<gt>> command). Fields:"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:597
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<run>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:602
msgid ""
"Required: I<builtin:E<lt>nameE<gt>> (I<minimize-others>, I<show-window>, "
"I<mirror>, I<terminal>) or a custom command — it is parsed by B<shlex>, "
"without a shell and without waiting."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:602
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<zone>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:607
msgid ""
"The subject zone: the window is looked for in it (the active one if it is "
"there, otherwise the topmost by I<_NET_CLIENT_LIST>). Without the field the "
"subject is the active window and the zone it stands in."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:607
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<key>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:611
msgid ""
"The Cinnamon hotkey for B<setup-hotkeys>; the hotkey name is \"zone-tiler: "
"action E<lt>nameE<gt>\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:611
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<command>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:615
msgid ""
"Only for I<builtin:terminal>: what to start the terminal with "
"(I<x-terminal-emulator> by default)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:615
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<axis>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:619
msgid ""
"Only for I<builtin:mirror>: the mirror axis, I<horizontal> (the default) or "
"I<vertical>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:626
msgid ""
"An empty field, an unknown field of the section, B<command> or B<axis> not "
"with its own action, an axis that is not in the list, a section name that is "
"not from I<[a-z0-9_-]> — a config error (code 3): a typo would leave a "
"person without an action or without a key. The editor does not edit the "
"section and carries it over verbatim, like B<[focus]>/B<[tabs]>."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: man/gridsnap.1:626
#, no-wrap
msgid "[workspaces]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:631
msgid ""
"The section is optional. A grid of its own per Cinnamon workspace: "
"I<workspace number = profile name> (EWMH numbering, from zero). The daemon "
"takes the grid by the window's workspace and does reflow only on the visible "
"workspace.  Edited in the editor (\"Workspace profiles…\")."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: man/gridsnap.1:631
#, no-wrap
msgid "[monitors]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:638
msgid ""
"The section is optional. A grid of its own per screen: I<output name = "
"profile name> (I<HDMI-1>, I<eDP-1>). The screen beats the workspace: "
"B<apply>/B<move>/B<arrange>/B<stack> look the zone up first in the screen "
"profile (B<[monitors]>), then the workspace one (B<[workspaces]>), then in "
"I<zones.conf>. The snapshot of the bindings is assembled into the active "
"config by B<profile use-monitors>, which is what autostart calls at session "
"start."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: man/gridsnap.1:638
#, no-wrap
msgid "[daemon]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:642
msgid ""
"The section is optional. B<reflow = off | neighbors> (I<off> by default; "
"case and spaces do not matter, an unknown value is treated as I<off>). The "
"I<neighbors> mode is described in the COMMANDS section."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: man/gridsnap.1:642
#, no-wrap
msgid "theme.conf"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:650
msgid ""
"An optional second INI file next to I<zones.conf>: one palette for the "
"surfaces GridSnap draws itself — the picker overlay, the hot-corners HUD, "
"the tab strip and the editor. The section B<[theme]> holds the switches, "
"B<[colors]> the colours (a colour in B<[theme]> is accepted too). Without "
"the file every surface keeps its built-in colours. Unknown keys are ignored; "
"a malformed value keeps the base colour and prints one warning on stderr, so "
"a typo never hides the grid."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:658
msgid ""
"Colours are I<#RRGGBB>: I<bg> (behind everything), I<bg_panel> (the tab "
"strip, the editor canvas), I<bg_card> (a tab, a button, an entry), "
"I<bg_hover> (the active tab, a hovered button), I<fg>, I<fg_muted>, "
"I<accent> (the selection, the active tab stripe, a checked button), "
"I<border>, I<danger>, I<ok>, and I<zones> — up to 16 zone colours separated "
"by commas; without I<zones> eight hues are derived from I<accent>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:664
msgid ""
"In B<[theme]>: B<preset> is one of I<43pr>, I<nord>, I<tokyo-night>, "
"I<catppuccin-mocha>, I<graphite> (the B<[colors]> values override whatever "
"the preset names); B<radius> is the zone corner radius in px, 0..64, I<10> "
"by default; B<font> is the Pango family of the labels, I<Sans> by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:670
msgid ""
"The editor's “From the wallpaper…” action writes this file from the desktop "
"picture and marks its first line as generated; the running daemon then "
"follows I<picture-uri> and rewrites the palette when the image "
"changes. Deleting the file — or removing that first line — returns the "
"built-in colours and stops the refresh."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:676
msgid ""
"The file does not theme window decorations: Muffin never reads a metacity "
"theme, so the borders of server-side decorated windows stay as it draws "
"them.  The editor can also write a GTK 3 controls theme with the same "
"palette; while its files carry the generated marker, the daemon keeps them "
"in step with the palette, and picking the theme in Cinnamon Settings is the "
"user's action."
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: man/gridsnap.1:676
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXAMPLES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:706
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"gridsnap-tiler list\n"
"gridsnap-tiler apply main --dry-run\n"
"gridsnap-tiler apply bottom --monitor 1 --verify\n"
"gridsnap-tiler arrange --by order\n"
"gridsnap-tiler stack main\n"
"gridsnap-tiler tabs-next\n"
"gridsnap-tiler undo --all\n"
"gridsnap-tiler focus main\n"
"gridsnap-tiler focus --off\n"
"gridsnap-tiler action mirror\n"
"gridsnap-tiler action term-main --dry-run\n"
"gridsnap-tiler profile save work\n"
"gridsnap-tiler profile use work --no-hotkeys\n"
"gridsnap-tiler profile gallery\n"
"gridsnap-tiler profile from-gallery work --name mine\n"
"gridsnap-tiler keys\n"
"gridsnap-daemon --verbose\n"
"gridsnap-daemon --once --conf ~/.config/gridsnap/zones.conf\n"
"gridsnap-ctl status\n"
"gridsnap-ctl apply main --monitor 1\n"
"gridsnap-ctl focus main\n"
"gridsnap-ctl focus --off\n"
"gridsnap-ctl watch\n"
"setup-hotkeys --list\n"
"gridsnap-picker --select top-right\n"
"gridsnap-picker --toggle\n"
"gridsnap-hotcorners --dry-run --verbose\n"
"gridsnap-editor --conf ~/.config/gridsnap/zones.conf\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: man/gridsnap.1:707
#, no-wrap
msgid "HOTKEYS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:713
msgid ""
"Hotkeys are set in the B<[keys]> section of I<zones.conf> and registered in "
"Cinnamon by the B<setup-hotkeys> command (or by a button in the editor) as "
"custom hotkeys named \"zone-tiler: E<lt>zoneE<gt>\" that run "
"B<gridsnap-tiler apply E<lt>zoneE<gt> --quiet>. After editing B<[keys]> by "
"hand you have to re-run B<setup-hotkeys>, otherwise the new zone names will "
"not be tied to keys."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:719
msgid ""
"The shipped I<zones.conf> has four zones and four hotkeys: I<main> — "
"I<E<lt>SuperE<gt>E<lt>AltE<gt>1>, I<top-right> — "
"I<E<lt>SuperE<gt>E<lt>AltE<gt>2>, I<top-far> — "
"I<E<lt>SuperE<gt>E<lt>AltE<gt>3>, I<bottom> — "
"I<E<lt>SuperE<gt>E<lt>AltE<gt>4>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:723
msgid ""
"The optional B<[focus]> section gives the key of \"only this zone\" mode "
"(B<gridsnap-tiler focus>): it is registered under the name \"zone-tiler: "
"focus\", so B<setup-hotkeys --remove> removes it together with the zone "
"keys."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:728
msgid ""
"The optional B<[tabs]> section gives the \"next window of the zone\" key "
"(B<gridsnap-tiler tabs-next>) under the name \"zone-tiler: tabs-next\". The "
"key switches tabs in the zone of the active window; without a running daemon "
"there is nothing to switch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:733
msgid ""
"The optional B<[overlay]> section gives the key that shows the zone grid "
"over the live desktop (B<gridsnap-picker --toggle>) under the name "
"\"zone-tiler: desktop grid\"; without the section the default "
"I<E<lt>SuperE<gt>g> is registered. The same key hides the grid again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:739
msgid ""
"B<[action:E<lt>nameE<gt>]> sections with a non-empty B<key> give action keys "
"under the name \"zone-tiler: action E<lt>nameE<gt>\": the command is "
"B<gridsnap-tiler action E<lt>nameE<gt> --quiet>, that is, the same path as "
"the zone keys. B<setup-hotkeys --remove> removes them together with the "
"rest."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:745
msgid ""
"Switching a profile with one key is an ordinary Cinnamon custom hotkey that "
"calls B<gridsnap-tiler profile use E<lt>nameE<gt>>: the project does not "
"create keys of its own for profiles.  A hotkey for B<gridsnap-picker> (for "
"example I<Super+Z>) is set up by the user himself — B<setup-hotkeys> "
"installs only the zone keys from B<[keys]>."
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: man/gridsnap.1:745
#, no-wrap
msgid "FILES"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:746
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<~/.config/gridsnap/zones.conf>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:751
msgid ""
"The active config (honouring I<$XDG_CONFIG_HOME>). If the file does not "
"exist, I<zones.conf> next to the code (I</usr/lib/gridsnap/zones.conf>) is "
"read and written."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:751
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<~/.config/gridsnap/theme.conf>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:757
msgid ""
"The optional palette of the GridSnap surfaces, in the directory of the "
"active I<zones.conf>. The editor writes it from the wallpaper and the daemon "
"keeps it in step while its first line says it was generated; deleting it "
"returns the built-in colours."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:757
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<~/.themes/Gridsnap>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:763
msgid ""
"The GTK 3 controls theme the editor writes (B<Window controls…> in the "
"B<Theme> menu). The daemon refreshes it from the current palette while its "
"files carry the generated marker; it must be selected in Cinnamon Settings, "
"Themes, Controls."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:763
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<~/.local/state/gridsnap/history.json>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:767
msgid ""
"The layout history (honouring I<$XDG_STATE_HOME>): JSON, the last 20 "
"operations, written atomically. Needed by B<undo> in a separate process."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:767
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/gridsnap/daemon.sock>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:771
msgid ""
"The daemon's UNIX socket (mode 0600, directory 0700). Without "
"I<$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR> — I</tmp/gridsnap-E<lt>uidE<gt>/daemon.sock>."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:771
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<~/.config/gridsnap/templates/*.conf>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:775
msgid ""
"Layout profiles (honouring I<$XDG_CONFIG_HOME>; with B<--conf> I<PATH> — the "
"I<templates> directory next to that file)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:775
#, no-wrap
msgid "I</usr/share/gridsnap/gallery/*.conf>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:780
msgid ""
"Ready-made layouts shipped with the package (in a checkout — I<gallery/> "
"next to the code). The I<$GRIDSNAP_GALLERY> variable sets a custom "
"directory. A copy of a layout into a profile is made by B<profile "
"from-gallery>; the directory itself is never modified."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:780
#, no-wrap
msgid "I</usr/lib/gridsnap>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:785
msgid ""
"The package code: I<zone-tiler.py>, I<zone-daemon.py>, I<zone-editor.py>, "
"I<zone-picker.py>, I<zone-tabstrip.py>, I<gridsnap-ctl>, I<setup-hotkeys.py> "
"and the helper modules, as well as the shipped I<zones.conf>."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:785
#, no-wrap
msgid "I</usr/bin/gridsnap-tiler>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:790
msgid ""
"The command launchers (I<gridsnap-tiler>, I<gridsnap-daemon>, "
"I<gridsnap-editor>, I<gridsnap-picker>, I<gridsnap-ctl>, I<setup-hotkeys>) — "
"wrappers around the code in I</usr/lib/gridsnap>."
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: man/gridsnap.1:790
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXIT STATUS"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:791
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<0>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:795
msgid ""
"Success. B<arrange> and B<stack> with no suitable windows and B<undo> with "
"an empty history are 0 too."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:795
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<1>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:801
msgid ""
"A runtime error: no display or no active window, I<_NET_CLIENT_LIST> not "
"read, the IPC socket could not be raised (daemon), no connection to the "
"daemon or the command was refused (B<gridsnap-ctl>), a B<gsettings>(1) error "
"(B<setup-hotkeys>)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:801
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<2>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:805
msgid ""
"An argument error: an unknown command or zone, a bad profile name, a wrong "
"flag.  It is reported by B<argparse> or by the command itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/gridsnap.1:805
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<3>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:811
msgid ""
"A config error: the file is missing, there is no zone at all, broken "
"numbers, fractions outside 0..1, a rule for an unknown zone, a missing or "
"broken profile. B<gridsnap-tiler> and B<gridsnap-daemon> answer like this; "
"B<gridsnap-picker> exits with code 1 in the same cases."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:815
msgid ""
"B<gridsnap-ctl> has codes 0, 1 and 2; B<gridsnap-daemon> — 0, 1 (socket) and "
"3 (config); B<gridsnap-editor> and B<gridsnap-picker> — 0 and 1 (plus 2 from "
"B<argparse>); B<setup-hotkeys> — 0, 1 and 2."
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: man/gridsnap.1:815
#, no-wrap
msgid "SEE ALSO"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:820
msgid ""
"B<gridsnap-tiler>(1), B<gridsnap-daemon>(1), B<gridsnap-editor>(1), "
"B<gridsnap-picker>(1), B<gridsnap-hotcorners>(1), B<gridsnap-ctl>(1), "
"B<setup-hotkeys>(1), B<man>(1), B<xprop>(1), B<xwininfo>(1), "
"B<gsettings>(1)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/gridsnap.1:822
msgid ""
"The package documentation is in I</usr/share/doc/gridsnap/> (README, SPEC "
"and I<docs/>)."
msgstr ""
